# front

Private Vite SPA. Add features under `src/`.

## Stack

- React 19 + TypeScript, bundled by Vite 8 (`@vitejs/plugin-react`)
- UI: MUI 9 with Emotion (`@mui/material`, `@emotion/react`, `@emotion/styled`)
- Routing: `react-router-dom` (`RouterProvider` in `src/routes`)
- Lint: ESLint flat config in `eslint.config.js` for `**/*.{ts,tsx}`

## Entry

`index.html` mounts `#root` → `src/main.tsx` (StrictMode) → `MainProvider` → `App` → `src/routes`. `MainProvider` only mounts `ThemeProvider`, `CssBaseline`, and `LanguageSwitch`. Language toggle, document `lang`/`dir`, and `localStorage` live in `src/language/config.ts` (`switchLanguage`, `nextLanguageLabel`). Static files go in `public/`.

## TypeScript

`tsconfig.app.json` covers `src`. Keep these constraints:

- `verbatimModuleSyntax`: use `import type` for types
- `allowImportingTsExtensions`: import local modules with `.ts` / `.tsx`
- `noUnusedLocals` / `noUnusedParameters`: delete unused symbols
- `erasableSyntaxOnly`: no enums; use unions and `as const`

## Commands

- `npm run dev` — Vite dev server
- `npm run build` — `tsc -b` then `vite build`
- `npm run lint` — ESLint
- `npm run preview` — serve the production build

## UI

Use functional components. Style with MUI (`sx` or `styled`) instead of new CSS files. Keep language and direction logic in `src/language/config.ts`. Do not put it in `MainProvider` or `main.tsx`.

```tsx
import Button from '@mui/material/Button'

export default function App() {
  return <Button variant="contained">Save</Button>
}
```
